id: pm-gh1390
title: "GH-1390: Keep trusted merge-receipt attribution and committed reconciliation authoritative"
description: The report describes receipt-attributable drift routed to history-repair and a reconciled durable receipt treated as pending by another worktree. Reproduce with real shared Git worktrees before modifying the reconciliation contract.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-04T11:45:54.908Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-07T08:10:45.470Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-07T08:00:32.210Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-07T08:00:32.210Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Trusted pending receipt overlap routes drift remediation to merge reconcile; Committed reconciled state dominates stale clone-local pending indexes; Repeated reconciliation writes nothing and adds no duplicate audit event; Unrelated drift and malformed evidence remain fail-closed.
goal: project management = context management
objective: Trustworthy bounded context and SDK-owned evidence
value: Agents can act on one truthful context read and preserve durable evidence
parent: pm-dj98
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Require exact immutable receipt provenance and matching sealed verified merge_reconcile disposition history before durable terminal state suppresses pending evidence. Preserve readonly scans, correct health attribution and idempotent interrupted settlement; document original HEAD and retained durable sidecars."
expected_result: "Audited committed settlement dominates stale local copies; absent, invalid or mismatched audit leaves durable evidence pending without writes, and supported SDK startup remains within existing budgets."
actual_result: "40 linked tests and all 9884 applicable tests pass with exact 100/100/100/100 source coverage. Four TypeScript projects, nine packed npx/bunx packages and installed Node/Bun recovery journeys pass. Isolated ten-entrypoint startup diagnostic has zero budget violations, runtime median 259ms against 452ms. Final complete static chain and hosted re-review remain landing gates; next daily publication remains separate."
affected_version: 2026.10.4
