comments[17]:
  - created_at: "2026-10-04T11:45:54.908Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Duplicate check: complete live all-status corpus returned 2873 of 2873 records with zero omissions. Exact GH-1390 and issue URL were absent. Full relevant terminal predecessor metadata and comments were inspected. Request-specific search and open/in-progress inventories were refreshed. This distinct reported boundary is retained under the existing lineage and remains open and unclaimed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T05:02:53.256Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Delivery scope: authoritative receipt lifecycle composition, shared-worktree drift attribution and idempotent reconciliation, implemented alongside pm-gh1405. TDD owner: real shared Git worktrees and persisted history/receipt bytes; retain malformed/mismatched proof rejection. Full all-status duplicate check is complete at 2901 records; no new umbrella or duplicate item. Only the two actively edited owners are in_progress."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T05:08:47.421Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "TDD red evidence: real linked Git worktree with durable-only lossless receipt has merge_receipt_attributed_items empty and generic history repair guidance. Regression also asserts committed settlement dominates stale local pending bytes and a second SDK reconciliation leaves history and both receipt copies byte-identical. Immutable provenance validation remains mandatory."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T05:10:59.902Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Additional TDD red: actual EACCES on durable receipt persistence occurs after the applied merge history audit commits. Retry appended a duplicate empty merge_reconcile event. The shared worktree keeper now requires byte-identical history across retry; the repair planner reuses only identical trusted receipt context, preserving force behavior and ordinary explicit audits."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T05:28:04.886Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Repository context verification: full live health and history-drift validation pass. Health retains 14 advisory legacy hierarchy findings; validation reports 170 historical resolution-field warnings rather than integrity failures. Complete all-status intake and graph census include terminal history; no fabricated depth or inferred closure evidence is added. GitHub has no open PRs before this delivery, all 23 open issues have PM-file comments, and native security alert inventories plus dependency audit are empty. These observations do not claim the wider open roadmap complete."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T06:08:02.591Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final canonical runner passes 9,884 applicable tests with two Windows-only platform skips and exact all-source 100/100/100/100 coverage. Four TypeScript projects passed. Packed npx/bunx smoke passes all nine bundled packages; independent installed Node/Bun recovery journeys pass. The staged secret scan identified one machine-specific npm path in delivery evidence, now removed through verified history-redact plus a normal comment correction; item/history integrity remains valid and the staged scan passes. Final static validation and hosted review remain pending."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T06:36:27.909Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "PR 1422 first reviewed source head 5d198b93d054ecbe2e73b159fcaa8eb312479218 passes every one of the 26 effective required contexts; GitHub reports CLEAN with no missing checks. Native Windows recovery, coverage, static/type checks, CodeQL, Trivy, ShellCheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, actionlint, CodeFactor, DeepScan and package/runtime matrices pass. Review inventory has no inline findings: CodeRabbit automatic review skipped due repository star policy and must be explicitly triggered; Greptile trial ended and Sourcery review quota is exhausted. These provider limitations are not clean code-review approvals. Every current bot artifact will receive a usefulness vote and a specific linked acknowledgement before the final metadata push/retrigger."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T06:40:51.695Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "First feedback round completed: all six bot artifacts were read in full, voted thumbs-up for useful scope/coverage/availability information, and given specific artifact-linked revision-aware acknowledgements; there were no inline threads. Sourcery guide and benchmark report are contextual evidence; trial/quota notices remain limitations. CodeRabbit full manual review is requested after the final PM correction push, together with the other configured providers. Production source, test inputs and all-source coverage denominator are unchanged from the green reviewed source head."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T06:57:24.766Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review remediation: CodeRabbit PR 1422 thread 4203949218 identifies a schema-valid durable reconciled flag without matching history audit suppressing pending evidence. The same unmerged canonical delivery is reopened for real-file negative controls and verified history-backed lifecycle authority; no duplicate work item is created."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T06:59:51.439Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review TDD red: the existing real linked-worktree keeper writes a schema-valid durable reconciled flag with no merge_reconcile audit; inspectMergeReceiptEvidence currently returns no pending receipts. The focused regression fails at the pending-evidence assertion, independently reproducing thread 4203949218. Coverage and gates are unchanged."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T07:03:41.401Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review remediation green: 35 focused SDK and real-Git integration tests pass. The primary worktree keeper now proves unaudited durable-only and paired-copy flags stay pending without file mutation, then checks valid settlement, interrupted retry and stale local copies. Additional controls preserve a valid sealed history chain while changing operation/context/summary, reject unsealed or damaged history, and distinguish applied from abandoned disposition. The direct receipt writer test retains raw persisted reconciled-state assertions while proving a lifecycle flag alone cannot settle fresh-clone evidence."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T07:26:24.168Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Full-run remediation evidence: the first review-fix coverage attempt found exactly three historical fixtures that used the receipt persistence primitive without an audit. Retained their undefined-slot, legacy/current hash, raw-byte and tamper controls; now settle real correctly matched item snapshots through runMergeReconcile. The missing-value fixture uses the actually absent optional assignee field. All six targeted compatibility/worktree cases pass; the complete exact-coverage runner is rerun next. No production gate or coverage denominator is relaxed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T07:48:31.258Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review-fix exact coverage passes all 9884 applicable tests across 784 files (two Windows-only skips on Linux): statements 67110/67110, branches 51377/51377, functions 13838/13838, lines 63952/63952. No exclusions or thresholds changed. The complete static chain passed source checks but correctly stopped at active expected-result metadata cleared by reopening; restored that required field through pm update and will rerun the full chain after final closure. Seven-file linked verification now passes."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T07:51:06.478Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final review remediation: all four TypeScript projects pass, packed npx/bunx smoke passes all nine bundled packages, and independently installed Node/Bun tarball journeys pass real Git conflict/abort, readonly abandonment planning, verified settlement, unaudited terminal-state visibility, byte-identical retries and typed preview refusal. Linked verification passes 40 cases in seven files; exact full coverage remains 9884 passing tests and 100/100/100/100. Second review round: all six new or revised bot artifacts were read, usefulness-voted and given specific revision-aware acknowledgements. CodeRabbit thread 4203949218 is fixed locally; final push, full hosted re-review and merge remain required. Live required Sentry/telemetry gate passes (3.24 percent finish errors, zero missing error codes); native security alerts remain zero. Latest registry pm-changelog remains 2026.10.5."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T07:59:13.112Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final static attempt passes metadata, source checks, graph and gate-registry checks but fails the required SDK runtime import-cost median: 515ms exceeds the unchanged 452ms budget. Investigate whether new eager history verification imports increased the entrypoint graph before rerunning; preserve the budget and use this unmerged canonical delivery rather than creating duplicate work."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T08:00:31.513Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Isolated fresh-process diagnostic used the unchanged benchmark implementation and budgets, five samples per entrypoint after warmup. All ten SDK entrypoints pass with zero violations: sdk/runtime p50 259ms, p95 300ms, unchanged allowed median 452ms. The earlier 515ms overshoot is not reproduced; host scheduling is a possible explanation, not a proven root cause. No source, benchmark, budget or coverage inputs changed. Repeat the full static chain once on final closed metadata; retain both receipts rather than erase the failed attempt."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T08:09:48.121Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final complete pnpm quality:static passes with final closed metadata: strict dependency/docstring/export/ESLint/duplicate checks, workflow permissions/cooldown, generated contracts and agent surfaces, package/SDK boundary and replication, command/refusal/token ratchets, tracker-context/graph/history assurance, gate registry, unchanged SDK entrypoint/startup budgets and bounded mutation checks. Four TypeScript projects, full exact coverage, linked 40-case keeper, installed Node/Bun and npx/bunx acceptance already pass on identical frozen source. Latest pm-changelog generation and check pass; all three implemented claims are released. The complete fix will be pushed for fresh exact-head hosted checks and all configured review requests on PR 1422; landing and publication are not claimed yet."
