  "2026-10-07T06:40:51.066Z","harness:codex","Chrome verification of PR 1422: DeepScan explicitly shows source head 5d198b93d054ecbe2e73b159fcaa8eb312479218 with 0 new and 0 fixed issues; CodeFactor PR report says No issues found. Its main dashboard separately retains two duplicate reports for generated standalone plugin scripts and canonical templates. Existing .codefactor.yml identifies these generated mirrors as the hosted Ignore Files checklist, and generation/replication gates remain mandatory. Do not describe a green no-new-issues PR check as zero total baseline findings; retain that baseline under the existing quality lineage pm-92if without inventing another duplicate owner."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T05:11:35.433Z","harness:codex","Committed durable lifecycle state must dominate stale worktree-local indexes only after exact immutable provenance validation. Retrying a history-committed, receipt-write-interrupted settlement must reuse its identical trusted audit context, while changed item proof and unrelated audits remain separate."
  "2026-10-07T07:48:31.953Z","harness:codex","Receipt copy provenance and lifecycle authority are separate proofs. A schema-valid terminal flag must not hide durable pending evidence: require its complete disposition summary in sealed, verified merge_reconcile history. Readonly scans verify history once per item and never rewrite damaged or unaudited evidence; exercise valid-chain wrong-context controls as well as malformed data."
